{"id": "EUVD-2026-59444", "enisaUuid": "4e5b176d-2f6a-351b-9d58-716796c34652", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/mlx5: Fix undefined shift of user RQ WQE size\n\nset_rq_size() computes the RQ WQE size as \"1 << rq_wqe_shift\" based on\nthe user-provided rq_wqe_shift, which is only checked to be greater than\n32, so shifts of 32 are still accepted. A shift of 31 also overflows a\nsigned integer, leading to undefined behavior.\n\nUse check_shl_overflow() to compute the RQ WQE size and reject any\ninvalid values.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:58:01", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:31", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9fff54929cc00849d738faa99f06c32399aeb026", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b746f949c2ac2b041102836095d6d4a2ef21fa75", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c1dbf52d24a8cb1aa56780ba51b72e7d495f258c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6fc874fdfb366bfb11c62e6af9a831c8be59ddda", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/42f3d2c8c18b92ea33e506a38b64f1a8986c2823", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4b87a2497276a72fd63028e7419abf0fb7ed837b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b732db02a2b04cde393638df19de6251ce62a74e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d881d60223aac8fdc12b227d89c76e131e92a9cd"], "aliases": ["GHSA-p4jx-gh49-76wv", "CVE-2026-74297"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "23be1760-3600-3b8c-bdce-7a459ed15ca5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "250c1c21-8d2c-36d3-9520-40b6865e8198", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.261"}, {"id": "26785c78-b54e-31ba-9044-a923c154d93f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e126ba97dba9edeb6fafa3665b5f8497fc9cdf8c <c1dbf52d24a8cb1aa56780ba51b72e7d495f258c"}, {"i